/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  unifacDortmund01_ethanol_water_reduced_pressure -- THE ORIGINAL UNIFAC AND
  THE MODIFIED (DORTMUND) UNIFAC, BOTH PREDICTIVE, AGAINST MEASURED VLE.

  THE QUESTION.  Ethanol + water is the textbook case where the original
  UNIFAC (Hansen 1991) misplaces the azeotrope.  The Dortmund model
  (Gmehling, Li & Schiller 1993) was fitted to VLE, excess enthalpies and
  infinite-dilution activity coefficients together, with a temperature-
  dependent interaction.  Does that show on a measured isobar the fit never
  saw?  Neither model is fitted to anything here; both are evaluated AT THE
  MEASURED x (the engine asked where the experimenter set the liquid, never a
  value read off a curve between grid points), and the residual is
  model(x_measured) - measurement.

  THE EVIDENCE.  Voutsas, Pamouktsis, Argyris & Pappa, Fluid Phase Equilib.
  308 (2011) 135-141, Table 1 (p. 137): isobaric ethanol(1) + water(2) VLE at
  13.15, 19.71 and 32.86 kPa -- T, x1, y1 of 15 + 16 + 14 interior points.
  Measured in 2011, so OUT OF SAMPLE for both group tables (1991 and 1993);
  the data files carry the page and the DOI.

  THE TWO MODELS.  `model UNIFAC;` is the original; `model UNIFACDortmund;` is
  the modified, with its parameters ONLY as printed in Gmehling et al. 1993
  Tables III-IV (data/standards/parameters/UNIFACDortmund/).  Each component's
  Dortmund decomposition is its own `groups { unifacDortmund (...) }` record
  (ethanol = CH3 + CH2 + OH_p, water = H2O), never the original's.

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pressure is 13-33 kPa, low enough for an ideal-gas
  vapour and the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records; part of every
  residual is those records' error at 307-345 K, identical for both models.  The
  Dortmund parameters were fitted mostly to 20-125 C data (the paper, p. 181);
  this range is inside it.  Which model is nearer is READ FROM THE aad ROWS
  OF `expected`, not asserted here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        txy_unifac_13p15;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        //  the 15 measured interior x of Table 1 at 13.15 kPa, in the paper's own order
        vary        { variable x[ethanol];
                      points ( 0.117 0.241 0.383 0.492 0.590 0.656 0.771 0.840 0.864 0.897 0.908 0.911 0.934 0.947 0.971 ); }
        state       { P 13.15 kPa;  composition { ethanol 0.5;  water 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model UNIFAC; } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_ethanol );
        output      { file txy_unifac_13p15.csv; }
    }
    {
        name        txy_dortmund_13p15;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        //  the 15 measured interior x of Table 1 at 13.15 kPa, in the paper's own order
        vary        { variable x[ethanol];
                      points ( 0.117 0.241 0.383 0.492 0.590 0.656 0.771 0.840 0.864 0.897 0.908 0.911 0.934 0.947 0.971 ); }
        state       { P 13.15 kPa;  composition { ethanol 0.5;  water 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model UNIFACDortmund; } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_ethanol );
        output      { file txy_dortmund_13p15.csv; }
    }
    {
        name        txy_unifac_19p71;
